Verified understanding of Pushgateway's persistence model and correct lifecycle management (push, scrape, delete) for metrics belonging to jobs that no longer exist
Conclusion
In this lab, you installed and configured both Prometheus and Pushgateway as systemd services, then built three realistic short-lived job scripts that pushed counters, gauges, and status metrics to Pushgateway using the text exposition format over HTTP. You configured Prometheus to scrape Pushgateway, verified end-to-end data flow with PromQL queries, and added alert rules to detect job failures, elevated error rates, and stale executions. Finally, you validated that Pushgateway persists pushed metrics across restarts and practiced the essential operational discipline of deleting stale metrics once a job's data is no longer relevant. You now understand both how to instrument ephemeral batch and cron-style workloads for Prometheus and how to manage the full lifecycle of pushed metrics in production.
